[(i)] For any subset $I=(I_{1},\cdots, I_{t})$ of $R$ and for any $z\in  T_{n-1}(\mathbb{Z})$ we introduce new tableau $\mathcal{D}_{I}T(v+z)$ which we call $I$-derivative tableau, or simply derivative tableau, and set $\mathcal{D}_{\emptyset}T(v+z) = T(v+z)$.

- [(ii)] Set $\tilde{V}(T(v))$ to be the complex vector space generated by $\{\mathcal{D}_{I}T(v+z)\; | \; I\subseteq R \text{ and } z\in  T_{n-1}(\mathbb{Z})\}$ subject to the following relations:

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{D}_{I}T(v+\tau_{r}(z))=
\begin{cases}
\mathcal{D}_{I}T(v+z), & \text{ if }\ \ \ \ \ \  I_{r}=\emptyset\\
-\mathcal{D}_{I}T(v+z), & \text{ if }\ \ \ \ \ \  I_{r}\neq\emptyset.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
